TITLE:: SampleCutter
summary:: a sample cut on the beat grid or on its attacks, written as a bank of its own
categories:: Libraries>SampleEditor
related:: Classes/SampleEditor, Classes/SampleEdit, Classes/SampleFeatures

DESCRIPTION::
The sample editor's slicer, usable on its own. The slices cover an
link::Classes/SampleEdit::'s trim: the first starts where the trim does, the
last ends where it ends. The cuts are on the edit's grid at a division, or on
the attacks its analysis heard at a sensitivity, and cuts made by hand stay on
top of either.

code::
e = SampleEdit("~/breaks.wav");
e.analyseFeatures;                       // the onsets, and a bpm for the grid
x = SampleCutter(e);
x.mode = \grid; x.division = 1/16;       // every sixteenth
x.numSlices;
x.mode = \transients; x.sensitivity = 0.7;
x.starts;                                // frames
x.addSliceAt(22050);
x.keepLevel = -18;                       // export only slices within 18 dB of the loudest
x.keepMinMs = 40;                        // and at least 40 ms long
x.numKept;
x.export;                                // a new folder beside the file, handed to the host
x.export(SampleCutter.samplesFolder +/+ "brk");   // brk/brk_00.wav ... in Dirt-Samples
::

Keep chooses which slices are exported, in either mode: those loud enough
(link::#-keepLevel::), long enough (link::#-keepMinMs::) and short enough
(link::#-keepMaxMs::), plus any put in by hand and minus any put out
(link::#-toggleKeepAt::). A slice that fails is dropped, not merged: its part
of the file is in no file, and the kept slices are numbered from 0 without
gaps. Every rule starts open, so keep changes nothing until it is set.

link::#-export:: writes every kept slice to a file of its own in a new folder
(code::_2::, code::_3:: when the name is taken), each file named after the
folder with the slice's index from 0, the code::n:: Tidal plays it as,
in the file's format, with the edit's gain and DC as set and short fades
(link::#*fadeInMs::, link::#*fadeOutMs::) so no cut clicks. The folder is
handed to the edit's host (link::Classes/SampleEditorHost#-folderWritten::):
a SuperDirt host loads it as a bank named after it. With a tag store, every
slice is tagged code::slice::, and on the grid given the grid's bpm. The sample itself is never written to.

It sends code::changed:: with code::\slices:: when the cuts change and
code::\exported:: with the folder.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: edit
an link::Classes/SampleEdit::; for transients mode, after its
link::Classes/SampleEdit#-analyseFeatures::.

METHOD:: divisions
What a grid offers: code::[[fraction of a whole note, name] ...]::, a bar down to
1/32, and triplets.

METHOD:: modes
code::[\grid, \transients]::.

METHOD:: levelOff
A link::#-keepLevel:: at or under this, -60 dB, keeps every level.

METHOD:: fadeInMs
METHOD:: fadeOutMs
Each slice's fades, 1 and 4 ms.

METHOD:: samplesFolder
Dirt-Samples, beside the SuperDirt quark: the folder SuperDirt's own
code::loadSoundFiles:: reads, so a bank exported there loads at every start.
RETURNS:: its path, or nil when it is not there.

METHOD:: exportParent
Where the editor's export went last; nil at first.

METHOD:: exportStart
Where the editor's export dialog opens: link::#*exportParent::, else
link::#*samplesFolder::, else the folder of the edit's file.
ARGUMENT:: edit
an link::Classes/SampleEdit::.

METHOD:: freeFolder
ARGUMENT:: parent
ARGUMENT:: name
RETURNS:: a path in parent that does not exist yet: the name, or the name with code::_2::, code::_3:: ...

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: mode
code::\grid:: or code::\transients::.

METHOD:: division
Of a whole note: 1/4 a beat, 1/16 a sixteenth.

METHOD:: sensitivity
0 .. 1, see link::Classes/SampleFeatures#*pickOnsets::.

METHOD:: minLength
Seconds: a cut closer than this to the one before, or to the end, is not made.

METHOD:: compute
The cuts again; every setter calls it, and the editor after the trim moves.
RETURNS:: link::#-starts::.

METHOD:: starts
The frames the slices start on, the trim's start first.

METHOD:: slices
code::[[start, end] ...]::, frames.

METHOD:: numSlices

METHOD:: gridStarts
METHOD:: transientStarts
Where each mode cuts, between two frames.
ARGUMENT:: f0
ARGUMENT:: f1

METHOD:: addSliceAt
A cut by hand.
ARGUMENT:: frame

METHOD:: removeSliceNear
Take away the cut nearest a frame, if there is one near enough; never the first.
ARGUMENT:: frame
ARGUMENT:: tolerance
frames; nil for 10 ms.
RETURNS:: true when one was taken away.

METHOD:: clearEdits
Forget the cuts made and taken away by hand, and the slices put in or out.

METHOD:: keepLevel
How far under the loudest slice a slice may be and still be kept, dB, from
link::#*levelOff:: to 0. A slice's level is its loudest 10 ms
(link::Classes/SampleEdit#-levelOf::), so a hit at the start of a long
slice counts, its tail does not pull it down.

METHOD:: keepMinMs
METHOD:: keepMaxMs
The shortest and the longest a kept slice may be, ms; 0 for no limit.

METHOD:: keepIsOn
Whether any rule is set or any slice put in or out by hand.

METHOD:: kept
Per slice, true when export writes it.

METHOD:: levels
Per slice, its level in dB under the loudest slice (0 for the loudest).

METHOD:: keptSlices
code::[[start, end] ...]:: of the kept slices, frames.

METHOD:: numKept
How many slices export writes.

METHOD:: sliceIndexAt
The slice a frame is in, or nil outside the trim.
ARGUMENT:: frame
a frame of the file.

METHOD:: toggleKeepAt
Put the slice a frame is in out of the export if it was in, in if it was out;
kept so whatever the rules say, through recomputes, until link::#-clearKeep::
or link::#-clearEdits::. cmd + click on the wave (ctrl on Windows and Linux).
ARGUMENT:: frame
a frame of the file.
RETURNS:: the slice's index, or nil.

METHOD:: forced
The slices put in or out by hand: code::[[start frame, kept] ...]::.

METHOD:: clearKeep
Forget the slices put in or out by hand; the cuts stay.

METHOD:: added
METHOD:: removed
The cuts by hand, frames.

METHOD:: defaultName
code::<file>_slices::, made a name SuperDirt takes as a bank's.

METHOD:: defaultFolder
link::#-defaultName:: beside the file, or the first free name after it.

METHOD:: fileNames
The names an export to a folder would give the kept slices: code::<folder>_00.wav::,
code::<folder>_01.wav:: ..., two digits or more, in the file's own extension.
ARGUMENT:: folder
a path; only its last part counts.

METHOD:: export
ARGUMENT:: folder
nil for link::#-defaultFolder::; a folder that exists gets a free name beside it.
ARGUMENT:: load
false writes the files and leaves the library alone.
RETURNS:: code::(folder:, paths:, bank:)::, or nil.

METHOD:: edit
METHOD:: sampleRate
The edit it cuts.
